    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff3cec9b</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>135.7982,34.6722,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Futai-ji Temple</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Nara &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>Nara temple, quiet old architecture and a pond garden.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff3cec9b</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>135.804,34.6883,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Takisaka no Michi</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Nara &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>Mossy stone trail through forest history near Nara; wear grip shoes.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff3cec9b</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>135.845,34.683,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Soni Highland</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Nara &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>Wide pampas-grass hills and sunset views in Nara; check bus times.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff3cec9b</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>136.086,34.518,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Mitarai Valley</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Nara &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>Clear river pools and gorge scenery in Nara.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff3cec9b</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>135.9,34.5,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Asuka Stone Monuments</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Nara &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>Ancient carved stones in rural Nara landscape, 6th-century era.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff3cec9b</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>135.8167,34.4667,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Dogo Onsen</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Ehime &middot; ★ &middot; off-spine<br/>Matsuyama, Ehime — oldest hot spring in Japan; inspired Spirited Away bathhouse. Ghibli real-world spot (off-mainland detour).]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff988f8a</color><scale>0.8</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>132.7850817,33.8504258,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Tomonoura</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Hiroshima &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>Hiroshima fishing village that inspired Ponyo's seaside town. Ghibli real-world spot.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff9eec3c</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>133.3803274,34.3808768,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Seiseki-Sakuragaoka</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Tokyo &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>Tokyo hillside town (Tama) that inspired Whisper of the Heart. Ghibli real-world spot.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff3c3cec</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>139.4470446,35.6508541,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Sayama Hills</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Saitama &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>Saitama wooded hills that inspired My Neighbor Totoro. Ghibli real-world spot.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff988f8a</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>139.3981823,35.7620951,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Nachi Falls</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Wakayama &middot; ★★★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>Japan's tallest single-drop waterfall (133m) and largest of the 48 Nachi Falls — sacred to Hiro Shrine, which worships the waterfall as its deity. Crest 13m, basin 10m deep, ~1 ton water/sec. Free view area, small fee for closest deck. Misty/otherworldly on rainy days.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff5eec3c</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>135.8876266,33.6752833,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Aogashima Island</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Tokyo &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>Remote volcanic island in the Izu chain; lush cliffs + turquoise water. Free to explore but need ferry/helicopter to reach. From 'Unreal places' slideshow.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff3c3cec</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>139.7674692,32.458249,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Hitachi Seaside Park</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Ibaraki &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>Seasonal flower fields (blue nemophila hills); small entrance fee, best season varies. From 'Unreal places' slideshow.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff988f8a</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>140.5943473,36.4025276,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Arashiyama Bamboo Forest</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Kyoto &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>Kyoto's iconic bamboo grove; free entry, best early morning. Real talk (Kyoto guide Naoya, 09-05): it looks stunning in photos but the actual walk is SHORT and way too crowded — low ROI. Consider Philosopher's Path (recommended) or Kibune instead.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff3cecdb</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>135.6711482,35.0167419,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Lake Kawaguchi</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Yamanashi &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>One of the best Mount Fuji view spots; free; beautiful in cherry-blossom and autumn seasons. From 'Unreal places' slideshow.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff3c7cec</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>138.7448243,35.5130603,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Ginzan Onsen</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Yamagata &middot; ★ &middot; off-spine<br/>Charming traditional hot-spring town, magical in winter; walking free, baths have entrance fee. From 'Unreal places' slideshow.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff988f8a</color><scale>0.8</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>140.5300687,38.5704194,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Oirase Gorge</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Aomori &middot; ★ &middot; off-spine<br/>Scenic 14km stream valley from Lake Towada; free walking trail, lush forest and waterfalls. From 'Unreal places' slideshow.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff988f8a</color><scale>0.8</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>140.9745,40.525278,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Takaragawa Onsen Osenkaku</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Gunma &middot; ★ &middot; off-spine<br/>Gunma riverside onsen (Minakami) — outdoor mixed rotenburo pools along a river in a misty forest; steam + traditional wooden buildings. From 'wake up to soft rain' onsen video.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff988f8a</color><scale>0.8</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>139.0468165,36.8479555,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Kegon Falls</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Tochigi &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>Nikko (Tochigi) — the real view is from the lower deck: take the underground elevator down (tunnel walk + reveal are part of it); ~$4 cash only. Top free lookout is the lesser view. Day-trip from Tokyo via Tobu Nikko Line (book direct trains 2+ wks ahead).]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff988f8a</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>139.5019683,36.7380094,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Shibuya Hikarie Sky Lobby</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Tokyo &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>Free 11F sky lobby 2 min from Shibuya station — huge-window view over Shibuya Crossing; great photos. Address: 2-21-1 Shibuya. Free Tokyo viewpoint (from Tokyo tour video).]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff3c3cec</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>139.7036853,35.6591803,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Tower Hall Funabori Observation Tower</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Tokyo &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>Free observation deck at 103m in Edogawa; hidden gem, no tourists — see Skytree, Tokyo Tower, Mt Fuji, whole city. Address: 4-1-1 Funabori. Free Tokyo viewpoint (from Tokyo tour video).]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff3c3cec</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>139.8649112,35.6843894,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Asakusa Culture Tourist Information Center</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Tokyo &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>Free 8F observation terrace steps from Kaminarimon — view over Sensoji Temple + Tokyo Skytree. Address: 2-18-9 Kaminarimon, Taito. Free Tokyo viewpoint.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff3c3cec</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>139.796528,35.710667,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Philosopher&#x27;s Path</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Kyoto &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>Kyoto canal-side walk; RECOMMENDED by guide Naoya — beautiful residential views esp. cherry-blossom and autumn seasons; great photos. (from 09-05 guide verdicts)]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff3cecdb</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>135.7963761,35.0247911,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Kibune</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Kyoto &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>Mountain village north of Kyoto; RECOMMENDED by guide Naoya — a bit far from the city but the best nature of Kyoto, cooler seasons (kawadoko river dining). (from 09-05 guide verdicts)]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff3cecdb</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>135.76425,35.1225862,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Eikando Temple</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Kyoto &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>Kyoto autumn spot #1 (guide Naoya): famous autumn foliage + night illumination/light show, very popular with locals. Trip is Oct — check foliage timing.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff3cecdb</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>135.790817,35.0146816,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Tofukuji Temple</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Kyoto &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>Kyoto autumn spot #2 (guide Naoya): spectacular autumn leaves over Tsutenkyo bridge; often compared to Fushimi Inari crowds but this is THE autumn-view temple.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff3cecdb</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>135.7736932,34.9760806,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Rurikoin Temple</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Kyoto &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>Kyoto autumn spot #3 (guide Naoya): autumn maple reflections on the polished table inside — REQUIRES reservation, limited entry.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff3cecdb</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>135.808589,35.0634463,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Shiraito Falls</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Shizuoka &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>UNESCO World Heritage waterfall near Mt. Fuji (part of the Fuji listing); featured in Fuji Soul Tours stopover itinerary. Fuji area day stop.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff3cbcec</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>138.5872234,35.312991,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Kitaguchi Hongu Fuji Sengen Shrine</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Yamanashi &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>The main shrine of Mt. Fuji (north base, Fujiyoshida); traditional starting point of the Fuji climb. Featured in Fuji Soul Tours stopover itinerary.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff3c7cec</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>138.7926376,35.4710138,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Fushimi Inari Taisha</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Kyoto &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>Iconic shrine with thousands of torii gates. Naoya's one-day route: GO 6-7am to beat the crowds (earlier he flagged it as too crowded LATER in the day — timing is everything).]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff3cecdb</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>135.7797101,34.9675192,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Kiyomizu-dera</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Kyoto &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>UNESCO temple in Higashiyama. Naoya one-day route: beautiful, but crowded — visit via the Higashiyama/Ninenzaka photo route. Was flagged 'too crowded' but route says worth it early.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff3cecdb</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>135.7844389,34.994303,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Gion District</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Kyoto &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>Kyoto's famous geisha/maiko district (Hanamachi). Naoya one-day route stop.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff3cecdb</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>135.778403,35.0046897,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Nishiki Market</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Kyoto &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>Kyoto's downtown covered food market ('Kyoto's kitchen'), 400yr old. Naoya one-day route: great lunch stop.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff3cecdb</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>135.7655699,35.0050244,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Nijo Castle</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Kyoto &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>UNESCO World Heritage castle, 400-year-old palace. Naoya one-day route: afternoon stop if energy remains.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff3cecdb</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>135.7485369,35.0140076,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Pontocho Alley</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Kyoto &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>Atmospheric dining/drinks alley by the Kamo River. Naoya one-day route: dinner + drinks end-of-day; kawadoko riverside dining this season.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff3cecdb</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>135.7712126,35.0042456,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Tarumizu Ruins</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Yamagata &middot; ★ &middot; off-spine<br/>Hidden otherworldly ruins next to Yamadera — honeycomb rock + torii, ~15 min walk off the approach path. From 'otherworld Japan' video.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff988f8a</color><scale>0.8</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>140.4431732,38.3179329,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Taki Shrine</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Gifu &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>Scenic shrine, breathtaking otherworld setting (in Gifu). From 'otherworld Japan' video.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff988f8a</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>136.8598652,35.6260122,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Kashima Jingu Shrine</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Ibaraki &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>One of Japan's most important/oldest shrines — powerful otherworld atmosphere. From 'hidden wonderland' otherworld video.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff988f8a</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>140.6260511,35.9706555,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Shipporyuji Temple</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Osaka &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>Hidden otherworld temple in the Osaka hills. From 'hidden wonderland' otherworld video.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff3cec5a</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>135.3877684,34.3383538,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Eiheiji Temple</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Fukui &middot; ★ &middot; off-spine<br/>Famous Soto Zen head temple in Fukui — forest setting. From 'hidden wonderland' otherworld video.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff988f8a</color><scale>0.8</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>136.3560152,36.0557075,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Sannobo Hie Shrine</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Aomori &middot; ★ &middot; off-spine<br/>Hie/Hiyoshi shrine in Aomori — otherworld forest setting. From 'hidden wonderland' otherworld video.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff988f8a</color><scale>0.8</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>140.3678921,41.06658,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Nene-no-Michi</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Kyoto &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>Scenic stone-paved path in Higashiyama, Kyoto (near Kiyomizu/Kodai-ji) with bamboo + lantern-lit atmosphere. Home of the summer Higashiyama Bamboo Light-Up (moon-viewing road) — but that light show runs JULY-AUG only, ended for our Oct trip. Street itself is lovely year-round.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ff3cecdb</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>135.77995,35.0005286,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Takasumi Shrine</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Fukuoka &middot; ★★ &middot; on-spine<br/>Mystical shrine at ~800m on the slopes of Mt. Hiko, Fukuoka — above-the-clouds scenery, magical in rain/mist. Featured in a DJI Pocket 4 cinematic video.]]></description>
    <Style><IconStyle><color>#ffdeec3c</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style>
    <Point><coordinates>130.9329879,33.4840463,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
